uncontrolled; CKD stage 2; medications listed include lisinopril 20 mg and amlodipine 5 mg; prior BP around 158/98.\\n- Current symptoms reported by patient: stress, fatigue, episodes of pounding/fast heartbeat lasting 2-3 minutes, and during episodes the patient says he can hardly breathe.\\n- Smartwatch/HRV data: resting HR 86 bpm; RMSSD 18.5 ms with severely depressed HRV; poor sleep 270-310 min/night; nocturnal BP 152-156/94-96; non-dipper/reverse-dipper; daytime HR 92-96 with peak 118-125; stress score 82-91; device alert for persistent nocturnal hypertension and flat HRV with high risk for renal/cardiac target-organ damage.\\n- Prior Doctor Agent assessment: symptoms should be taken seriously; possible stress-related palpitations but cannot safely exclude intermittent arrhythmia or other cardiovascular strain; urgent same-day evaluation recommended; emergency care warranted if symptoms are active or recur with chest pain, severe breathlessness, fainting, marked dizziness, neurologic symptoms, or sustained fast heartbeat.\\n\\nInstructions:\\n- Produce a clean Telegram-friendly medical report.\\n- Clearly separate: summary of current situation, supporting data, likely explanations, dangerous alternatives, urgency, and next-step plan.\\n- Keep uncertainty visible; do not present a confirmed diagnosis.\\n- Do not prescribe medication changes or dosages.\\n- End with a brief practical checklist the patient can use right away.\\n- Write it as a comprehensive but concise medical report for the patient.\",\"cwd\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-patient-agent\",\"runTimeoutSeconds\":120,\"timeoutSeconds\":120,\"mode\":\"run\",\"cleanup\":\"delete\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":4029,"output":521,"cacheRead":20352,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":24902,"cost":{"input":0.010072500000000002,"output":0.007815,"cacheRead":0.005088,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0229755}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":17758410165