310 minutes/night**\n- nighttime BP around **152–156 / 94–96**\n- **non-dipper / reverse-dipper** BP pattern\n- device warning for **persistent nocturnal hypertension** and possible **renal/cardiac strain**\n\n**Main concern**\nI want evaluation for whether this could be **palpitations from stress** versus an **intermittent arrhythmia or other cardiovascular problem**, especially because of the **shortness of breath** during episodes.\n\n**Useful checks to consider**\n- **ECG / rhythm assessment**\n- **blood pressure and pulse review**\n- **electrolytes and kidney function**\n- possible **ambulatory rhythm monitoring** if episodes are intermittent\n\nIf you want, I can make this into an even shorter **ER-style version** in 3–4 lines.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0e230605dcec22620169d92f9fbc288191a99fdebd925b8533\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":3235,"output":381,"cacheRead":24192,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":27808,"cost":{"input":0.008087500000000001,"output":0.0057150000000000005,"cacheRead":0.0060479999999999996,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0198505}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1775841181072}}
